      "message": "The device tree explicitly names OTG in recovery.fstab:\n\n  /devices/platform/mt_usb* /usb-otg auto ... display\u003d\"USB OTG\",storagename\u003d\"USB OTG\"\n\n  But TWRP handles sysfs wildcard storage in two stages. It first creates a parent entry like /usb-\n  otg, then discovers real block-device children such as /usb-otg-1 for /dev/block/sda1.\n\n  The original code did not preserve the explicit USB OTG name correctly when creating that child\n  entry. After that, Translate_Partition_Display_Names() treated it like generic removable storage\n  and renamed it back into the generic Storage naming scheme.\n\n  That caused the behavior you saw:\n\n  - Select Storage showed Storage (XXXMB) instead of USB OTG (XXXMB).\n  - Mount did not directly show a useful USB OTG mount item until selecting storage.\n  - The storage picker also showed parent placeholder entries like Storage (0MB) / Internal Storage\n    (0MB).\n\n  So the source code was not globally broken, but it was too generic for this fstab/sysfs case. The\n  fix preserves explicit labels like USB OTG and Micro SDCard for sysfs-discovered child partitions,\n  while still allowing Translate_Partition_Display_Names() to rename truly generic storage entries.",
